  "next_action": "Merge the Phase E PR after CI, then remediation 7: the comprehensive plan audit (reconciled inventory, directive statuses, semantic checks, reruns from pinned inputs incl. PB-AUD-08, negative controls, fresh receipt).",
  "sections": {
    "review": {
      "summary": "Inspected the existing feature registry (arbit_model.feature_specs: FEATURES with definitions, units, windows, sources and SHRINKAGE constants; legacy DvP columns opp_dvp_{QB..K}_{pg,pg_shrunk,adj,adj_shrunk,opps_pg} and opp_off_dst_allowed_*) and its consumers (team_features only; no production model assembles them). Collected each feature's evidence from the committed receipts (reliability-results A05/A07, backtest receipts, sitstart, league v2, explore-v3, simulation-v1, threshold-sensitivity-v1). Verified the owner-registered deploy key from the timer's service context (AUD-01a).",
      "files": [
        "libs/arbit-model/src/arbit_model/feature_specs.py",
        "docs/research/dvp/reliability-results.json"
      ]
    },
    "plan": {
      "summary": "1) A machine-readable registry (config/model/research-eligibility.json) with the directive's fields and initial classifications. 2) arbit_model.eligibility: load with validation (required fields, evidence kinds, classifications, no production eligibility without recorded approvals), governing() by entry id, feature_specs patterns and estimator columns, check_assembly failing closed for production and reporting for research. 3) Tests. 4) feature_specs note and an AGENTS.md rule pointing production assembly at the gate; no feature activated, no constant changed. 5) Docs and records; close AUD-01a.",
      "files": [
        "config/model/research-eligibility.json",
        "libs/arbit-model/src/arbit_model/eligibility.py"
      ]
    },
    "implementation": {
      "summary": "config/model/research-eligibility.json (10 entries); arbit_model/eligibility.py (load, governing, check_assembly, classifications, covered; RegistryError, IneligibleFeature; DVP_LIKE pattern for unregistered DvP-like names); feature_specs docstring note; AGENTS.md rule.",
      "files": [
        "config/model/research-eligibility.json",
        "libs/arbit-model/src/arbit_model/eligibility.py",
        "libs/arbit-model/src/arbit_model/feature_specs.py",
        "AGENTS.md"
      ]
    },
    "validation": {
      "summary": "All seven checks pass. test_eligibility.py (6): the directive's classifications recorded and nothing production-eligible; every legacy DvP feature_specs column governed and every registry pattern matching a real column; legacy shrinkage constants unchanged; production assembly refuses legacy columns, estimator columns, entry ids and unregistered DvP-like names while passing other features; research use reports; a registry claiming eligibility without recorded approvals, or with a missing evidence kind or unknown classification, fails to load. AUD-01a verified live: deploy key read-write, systemd-run publication over SSH with read-back and GitHub timestamp.",
      "files": [
        "libs/arbit-model/tests/test_eligibility.py"
      ]
    },
    "documentation": {
      "summary": "RESEARCH_ELIGIBILITY.md; MODEL_CARD.md eligibility note; DvP README; audit-findings.json (AUD-01a resolved, eligibility requirement resolved) and AUDIT_RECONCILIATION.md; decision register ENG-070; AGENTS.md rule; feature_specs note; status; changelog; next action.",
